CAT = "aesiraAccess"; SEG = "ACC"
Q = [
("What is the main purpose of access control at an office tower entrance?",
 "Only authorised people get in", ["Counting daily visitor footfall", "Selling parking tickets", "Checking visitors' dress codes"],
 "Access control lets authorised people and vehicles in and keeps others out, and records who entered and when."),
("A visitor arrives to see a tenant on the 30th floor. What should the guard do before issuing a visitor pass?",
 "Check ID and call the host", ["Issue the pass straight away", "Ask the visitor's nationality", "Send them up to find the host"],
 "The guard verifies identity and confirms the visit with the host, then records it. Sending unknown visitors up unchecked defeats access control."),
("A man in a courier uniform says he must deliver to an office in person, but has no booking. The guard should:",
 "Verify with the office first", ["Let him in, as couriers are safe", "Refuse all couriers", "Ask him to leave the parcel outside"],
 "Uniforms and parcels are easy to fake. Checking with the recipient confirms the visit without refusing genuine deliveries."),
("What is 'tailgating' at a controlled door?",
 "Slipping in behind a pass holder", ["Parking too close behind a car", "Leaving a door propped open", "Using someone else's expired pass"],
 "Tailgating (piggybacking) is entering behind an authorised person without using one's own credential. Guards watch turnstiles and doors for it."),
("A visitor pass should be collected back from a visitor:",
 "When they leave", ["After a week", "Only if they ask", "At the end of the month"],
 "Collecting passes on exit confirms the visitor has left and stops passes being reused by someone else."),
("Which detail is normally recorded in a visitor register?",
 "Name, host and times", ["Their monthly salary", "Home country address", "Their marital status"],
 "A register records who came, whom they visited and when they arrived and left, which helps in an evacuation or investigation."),
("An employee shows a staff card with a photo that clearly does not match their face. The guard should:",
 "Hold entry and call a supervisor", ["Let them in if they insist firmly", "Keep the card and say nothing", "Wave them in to avoid delay"],
 "A mismatched ID may be a borrowed or stolen card. The guard holds entry and escalates. Confiscating cards without authority is not appropriate."),
("A guard has walked the same car park route at 1, 2 and 3 a.m. every night for a month. What is the main risk?",
 "Offenders can time their entry", ["The tags will wear out sooner", "The shift will feel too long", "The client will cut the hours"],
 "A fixed routine lets someone watching the site slip in between rounds. Varying the route and timing keeps the patrol unpredictable."),
("On a night patrol, a guard finds a warehouse door unlocked that is normally locked. What should the guard do first?",
 "Look for signs of entry first", ["Walk straight in to search", "Lock it and say nothing at all", "Leave it for the morning shift"],
 "The guard observes first for signs of forced entry or intruders, then reports and calls for help before entering. Walking in alone may mean meeting an intruder."),
("A guard's patrol reaches a checkpoint tag that must be scanned. What does the scan prove?",
 "The guard visited that point", ["The area is free of fire risk", "All doors are locked", "No visitors came that night"],
 "Electronic patrol tags record when a guard was at each checkpoint. They do not show that every hazard was checked; the guard still has to look."),
("When patrolling a car park at night, the guard should:",
 "Look for damage and loiterers", ["Stay in one well-lit corner", "Stay on the phone throughout", "Patrol only near the exit gate"],
 "A car park patrol covers the area, watching for damaged vehicles, open windows, suspicious people and lighting faults, and reporting them."),
("Which patrol method lets a guard see and hear most of the surroundings?",
 "A patrol on foot", ["Patrolling with earphones", "Watching only from the car", "Staying in the guard room"],
 "Foot patrols let the guard hear, smell and see detail such as broken glass, gas leaks or voices. Earphones block warning sounds."),
("A contractor arrives with a work permit for the roof plant room. What should the guard check?",
 "Its date, area and name", ["The contractor's salary", "Their mobile phone model", "That they speak Arabic"],
 "A work permit is valid only for the named person, area and time. Checking all three stops unauthorised work in restricted areas."),
("A guard holds the key register for a site. What must be recorded when a key is issued?",
 "Who took it and when", ["The key's colour only", "The weather that day", "The cost of the key"],
 "A key log records the key, the person, the time out and the time back, so every key can be traced at any moment."),
("A lost key card is reported by a tenant. The best action for the guard is to:",
 "Have the card cancelled now", ["Wait for it to be returned", "Reissue the same card number", "Note it at month end"],
 "A lost credential is cancelled straight away so whoever finds it cannot use it. A new card is then issued through the proper procedure."),
("A delivery vehicle wants to enter a restricted loading bay. What is the guard's main check?",
 "That the delivery is expected", ["That the van is a new model", "That the driver is friendly", "That the van looks clean inside"],
 "The guard confirms the delivery is booked or expected and that the driver and vehicle match the details before opening the barrier."),
("A guard sees a person photographing the emergency exits and security cameras of a bank branch. What should the guard do?",
 "Note details and report it", ["Seize the camera by force", "Ignore it as normal tourism", "Chase the person away"],
 "This can be hostile reconnaissance. The guard notes the person, time and vehicle and reports it to the supervisor and, if needed, the police."),
("A resident asks the guard to let a 'cousin' into their empty flat while they are abroad. The guard should:",
 "Refuse without written authority", ["Open the door, as family is fine", "Open it if the cousin pays", "Give the cousin a spare key"],
 "Without written authority from the owner and the building's procedure, the guard cannot let anyone into private property."),
("Turnstiles and barriers at a site are mainly used to:",
 "Make each person show a pass", ["Count cars for traffic police", "Speed people through queues", "Stop evacuation"],
 "Physical barriers force each person to present a valid credential. In an emergency they must release so people can escape."),
("At an event entrance, a person refuses a bag check that is a published condition of entry. The guard should:",
 "Politely refuse them entry", ["Search the bag by force", "Let them in to avoid a fuss", "Take the bag and keep it"],
 "A search is by consent. If someone declines, the guard can refuse entry under the site's conditions, but must not search by force."),
("During a bag check at entry, the guard should ask the visitor to:",
 "Open the bag themselves", ["Hand over their wallet", "Empty pockets onto the floor", "Remove their shoes outside"],
 "Asking the owner to open and move items keeps the search consensual and respectful, and reduces claims of loss or damage."),
("While searching a bag at an event, a guard finds an item that may be illegal. What should the guard do?",
 "Hold entry and call the police", ["Take it and let them go in", "Destroy the item on the spot", "Let the person in without fuss"],
 "Guards are not police. Suspected illegal items are referred to Dubai Police; the guard records details and stops the person entering."),
("A female visitor must be searched at a venue entrance. Who should carry out the search?",
 "A female officer", ["Any guard on shift", "The visitor's companion", "The venue's manager"],
 "Personal searches are carried out by an officer of the same sex, respecting privacy and local custom. If none is available, ask for one."),
("Why must a guard check that emergency exits on a patrol route are clear?",
 "People must escape quickly", ["To store pallets there", "To lock them at night", "To use them as smoking areas"],
 "Blocked exits cost lives in a fire. Any obstruction is cleared if safe or reported straight away."),
("CCTV at a site works best when:",
 "Guards watch it and respond", ["The cameras are hidden only", "It records without anyone checking", "Monitors face the public"],
 "Cameras are only useful if someone watches and acts. Recordings also need checking that they are working and correctly timed."),
("A security systems monitor sees an alarm on the control panel for a fire exit door. What should happen first?",
 "View the camera and send a guard", ["Reset the panel and ignore it", "Switch the alarm off for the night", "Wait for a second alarm"],
 "Each alarm is treated as real until checked. The monitor views the area and sends a guard; resetting without checking may miss an intrusion."),
("A tenant asks the control room for a copy of CCTV footage of a car park argument. The guard should:",
 "Follow the release procedure", ["Send it by WhatsApp", "Post it to the building group", "Delete it to avoid trouble"],
 "Footage is released only through the site's procedure, normally to the police or an authorised person. Sharing it privately can breach UAE privacy law, and deleting it destroys evidence."),
("A guard must check a vehicle at a residential compound gate. Who should open the boot?",
 "The driver", ["The guard, without asking", "A passer-by", "Nobody, ever"],
 "The driver opens the boot with consent so the guard can look. A guard does not force a vehicle search."),
("A person loiters near a jewellery shop in a mall for a long time, watching staff. What should the guard do?",
 "Keep watch and inform control", ["Ask them to show their passport", "Remove them from the mall", "Ignore them until a crime"],
 "Watching openly deters an offender and gathers detail. A guard has no power to demand a passport or expel someone for loitering alone."),
("At closing time, the guard's lock-up check should include:",
 "Doors, windows and anyone inside", ["The staff canteen's stock levels", "The background music volume", "Customer reviews online"],
 "A lock-up confirms all doors and windows are secure, alarms are set and nobody is left inside, such as someone hiding in toilets."),
("A man claims to be a SIRA inspector and asks to see the site's records. What should the guard do?",
 "Check his ID and tell a supervisor", ["Refuse him entry without asking", "Hand him all the files at once", "Ask him to come back again next month"],
 "SIRA inspectors may inspect systems and records at any time, but the guard first confirms identity, since impostors use the same claim."),
("A guard sees a gap in a perimeter fence of a construction site. What should the guard do?",
 "Report it and watch the area", ["Climb through to test it", "Ignore it until morning", "Cover it with a cardboard sheet"],
 "A breach in the perimeter is reported for repair and watched more often until fixed, since it is an easy way in for intruders."),
]
